# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "Learn the noise model of a gate for the latest version of Qiskit noise learning"
msgstr "Apprendre le modèle de bruit d'une porte, pour la dernière version de Qiskit noise learning"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Learn the noise model of a gate"
msgstr "Apprendre le modèle de bruit d'une porte"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title #
#, no-wrap
msgid "Learn the noise model of a gate {#learn-the-noise-model-of-a-gate}"
msgstr "Apprendre le modèle de bruit d'une porte {#learn-the-noise-model-of-a-gate}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This tutorial demonstrates learning a noise model for a unitary gate with a standard learning protocol accessible through the high-level protocol functions [`prepare_vanilla_program()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-noise-learning/generated/protocols-prepare-vanilla-program#qiskit_noise_learning.protocols.prepare_vanilla_program \"qiskit_noise_learning.protocols.prepare_vanilla_program\") and [`process_vanilla_result()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-noise-learning/generated/protocols-process-vanilla-result#qiskit_noise_learning.protocols.process_vanilla_result \"qiskit_noise_learning.protocols.process_vanilla_result\").\n"
msgstr "Ce tutoriel montre comment apprendre un modèle de bruit pour une porte unitaire avec un protocole d'apprentissage standard accessible via les fonctions de protocole de haut niveau [`prepare_vanilla_program()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-noise-learning/generated/protocols-prepare-vanilla-program#qiskit_noise_learning.protocols.prepare_vanilla_program \"qiskit_noise_learning.protocols.prepare_vanilla_program\") et [`process_vanilla_result()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-noise-learning/generated/protocols-process-vanilla-result#qiskit_noise_learning.protocols.process_vanilla_result \"qiskit_noise_learning.protocols.process_vanilla_result\").\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '1.  '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Define the gate\n"
msgstr "Définir la porte\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '2.  '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Set up local simulation\n"
msgstr "Configurer la simulation locale\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '3.  '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Prepare the quantum program\n"
msgstr "Préparer le programme quantique\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '4.  '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Run the quantum program\n"
msgstr "Exécuter le programme quantique\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '5.  '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Read the results\n"
msgstr "Lire les résultats\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Running on real hardware\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  The circuits below are simulated locally, so this walkthrough needs no IBM Quantum® credentials. To alternatively run it on a real device:\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Exécution sur du matériel réel\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Les circuits ci-dessous sont simulés localement, donc ce pas à pas ne nécessite aucun identifiant IBM Quantum®. Pour l'exécuter plutôt sur un appareil réel :\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '  *   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Step 1**: replace [`FakeMarrakesh`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/fake-provider-fake-marrakesh \"(in Qiskit Runtime IBM Client)\") with a real backend.\n"
msgstr "**Étape 1** : remplace [`FakeMarrakesh`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/fake-provider-fake-marrakesh \"(in Qiskit Runtime IBM Client)\") par un vrai backend.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  *   **Step 2**: pass that backend as the executor’s mode, and drop the simulator options.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"  *   **Étape 2** : passe ce backend comme mode de l'executor, et supprime les options du simulateur.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"define-the-gate\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "1. Define the gate {#1-define-the-gate}"
msgstr "1. Définir la porte {#1-define-the-gate}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The gate is a [`BoxOp`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.BoxOp) holding a twirled layer of six disjoint `CZ` gates.\n"
msgstr "La porte est un [`BoxOp`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.BoxOp) contenant une couche twirlée de six portes `CZ` disjointes.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<DoqAdmonition type=\"note\" title=\"Running on real hardware\">\n"
msgstr "<DoqAdmonition type=\"note\" title=\"Exécution sur du matériel réel\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "</DoqAdmonition>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"set-up-local-simulation\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "2. Set up local simulation {#2-set-up-local-simulation}"
msgstr "2. Configurer la simulation locale {#2-set-up-local-simulation}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Pauli indices inside each map are local to the gate, in ascending physical-qubit order:\n"
msgstr "Les indices de Pauli à l'intérieur de chaque map sont locaux à la porte, dans l'ordre croissant des qubits physiques :\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Define the noise with a correlated `ZZ` term and a weaker `XX` term on each `CZ` pair, plus a single-qubit `Z` term everywhere; measurement gets a bit-flip term per qubit.\n"
msgstr "Définis le bruit avec un terme `ZZ` corrélé et un terme `XX` plus faible sur chaque paire `CZ`, plus un terme `Z` à un seul qubit partout ; la mesure reçoit un terme de bit-flip par qubit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Build a box for measurement to learn.\n"
msgstr "Construis une boîte que la mesure doit apprendre.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Each entry of `layer_noise_model` pairs one of those boxes with the map to apply to it. Use the stabilizer simulation method, and set `seed_simulator` to make the simulated data reproducible.\n"
msgstr "Chaque entrée de `layer_noise_model` associe une de ces boîtes à la map à lui appliquer. Utilise la méthode de simulation stabilizer et définis `seed_simulator` pour rendre les données simulées reproductibles.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"prepare-the-quantum-program\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "3. Prepare the quantum program {#3-prepare-the-quantum-program}"
msgstr "3. Préparer le programme quantique {#3-prepare-the-quantum-program}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Use [`prepare_vanilla_program()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-noise-learning/generated/protocols-prepare-vanilla-program#qiskit_noise_learning.protocols.prepare_vanilla_program \"qiskit_noise_learning.protocols.prepare_vanilla_program\") to build the quantum program containing the learning experiments.\n"
msgstr "Utilise [`prepare_vanilla_program()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-noise-learning/generated/protocols-prepare-vanilla-program#qiskit_noise_learning.protocols.prepare_vanilla_program \"qiskit_noise_learning.protocols.prepare_vanilla_program\") pour construire le programme quantique contenant les expériences d'apprentissage.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"run-the-quantum-program\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "4. Run the quantum program {#4-run-the-quantum-program}"
msgstr "4. Exécuter le programme quantique {#4-run-the-quantum-program}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Submit the quantum program. This step is the same whether the executor is pointed at a simulator or at a real device.\n"
msgstr "Soumets le programme quantique. Cette étape est la même que l'executor pointe vers un simulateur ou vers un appareil réel.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"read-the-results\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "5. Read the results {#5-read-the-results}"
msgstr "5. Lire les résultats {#5-read-the-results}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Process the result with [`process_vanilla_result()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-noise-learning/generated/protocols-process-vanilla-result#qiskit_noise_learning.protocols.process_vanilla_result \"qiskit_noise_learning.protocols.process_vanilla_result\").\n"
msgstr "Traite le résultat avec [`process_vanilla_result()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-noise-learning/generated/protocols-process-vanilla-result#qiskit_noise_learning.protocols.process_vanilla_result \"qiskit_noise_learning.protocols.process_vanilla_result\").\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Plot per-qubit-pair fidelity decays: both the data and the exponential fit.\n"
msgstr "Trace les décroissances de fidélité par paire de qubits : à la fois les données et l'ajustement exponentiel.\n"
